00:38:00.130 --> 00:38:04.920
And in retrospect it all looks so obvious,
they're upsetting the hotel industry and

00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:05.610
all the rest of it.

00:38:05.610 --> 00:38:10.360
But at the time that we met the company,
it was three young

00:38:10.360 --> 00:38:15.720
founders who were sort of
sleeping on airbeds, and

00:38:15.720 --> 00:38:19.440
it was sort of pigeonholed
this very niche service,

00:38:19.440 --> 00:38:23.170
it's the young people who
would have ever imagine.

00:38:23.170 --> 00:38:30.146
And I can point to any number of
other investments that seems similar.

00:38:30.146 --> 00:38:34.768
To me it's, with year, years ago,
a Stanford, this was a yet

00:38:34.768 --> 00:38:40.850
another offshoot of the incredible fertile
Stanford campus when we invested in Young.

00:38:40.850 --> 00:38:44.360
The idea of investing in a company
that gave its service away for

00:38:44.360 --> 00:38:49.810
free this is 1995, was totally foreign.

00:38:49.810 --> 00:38:50.840
Came out of left field.

00:38:52.180 --> 00:38:54.770
So it's those investments,

00:38:54.770 --> 00:38:59.570
the ones that aren't the obvious ones
that are the really interesting ones.

00:38:59.570 --> 00:39:06.500
We invested some years ago when in TJI
in which is a drone company, in China.

00:39:06.500 --> 00:39:11.860
Nobody imagined that the time that
we invested to do I think it did,

00:39:11.860 --> 00:39:13.350
